{"content":[{"c":["GERSHON, GERSHONITES"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Levi’s oldest son (also spelled Gershom) who went into Egypt with Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.11","r":"Gen.46.11","rawR":"Gen.46.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.11","value":"Gen.46.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 46:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.3.17","r":"Num.3.17","rawR":"Num.3.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.3.17","value":"Num.3.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 3:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.1","r":"1Chr.6.1","rawR":"1Chr.6.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.1","value":"1Chr.6.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:1"},") and was ancestor of a division of Levites (Gershonites) who came out of Egypt with Moses (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.6.16-17","r":"Exod.6.16-17","rawR":"Exod.6.16-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.6.16-17","value":"Exod.6.16-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 6:16-17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.3.18,21","r":"Num.3.18,21","rawR":"Num.3.18,21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.3.18,21","value":"Num.3.18,21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 3:18, 21"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In the list of the allotment of Levitical cities, the Gershonites were listed as one of the largest Levitical groups in Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.1-7","r":"Josh.21.1-7","rawR":"Josh.21.1-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.1-7","value":"Josh.21.1-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 21:1-7"},"). Some passages indicate that they were at times dominant among the functioning Levitical groups (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.11","r":"Gen.46.11","rawR":"Gen.46.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.11","value":"Gen.46.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 46:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.6.16","r":"Exod.6.16","rawR":"Exod.6.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.6.16","value":"Exod.6.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 6:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.3.17","r":"Num.3.17","rawR":"Num.3.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.3.17","value":"Num.3.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 3:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.57","r":"Num.26.57","rawR":"Num.26.57","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.57","value":"Num.26.57"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:57"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.1,16","r":"1Chr.6.1,16","rawR":"1Chr.6.1,16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.1,16","value":"1Chr.6.1,16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:1, 16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.23.6","r":"1Chr.23.6","rawR":"1Chr.23.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.23.6","value":"1Chr.23.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"23:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["According to the book of Numbers, the Gershonites were encamped behind the tabernacle to the west during the wilderness wanderings (",{"href":"?bref=Num.3.23","r":"Num.3.23","rawR":"Num.3.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.3.23","value":"Num.3.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 3:23"},"). Early in the second year after the exodus from Egypt, the Gershonite males numbered about 7,500 (v ",{"href":"?bref=Num.3.22","r":"Num.3.22","rawR":"Num.3.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.3.22","value":"Num.3.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"22"},"). Only those between the ages of 30 and 50 could serve in the tabernacle, which at the time of that early census totaled 2,630 men (",{"href":"?bref=Num.4.39-40","r":"Num.4.39-40","rawR":"Num.4.39-40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.4.39-40","value":"Num.4.39-40"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:39-40"},"). They were responsible for the care and transportation of the external furnishings of the tabernacle (",{"href":"?bref=Num.3.25-26","r":"Num.3.25-26","rawR":"Num.3.25-26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.3.25-26","value":"Num.3.25-26"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:25-26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.4.24,27-28","r":"Num.4.24,27-28","rawR":"Num.4.24,27-28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.4.24,27-28","value":"Num.4.24,27-28"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:24, 27-28"},") and were given two wagons and four oxen for the purpose, being supervised by Aaron and his sons (",{"href":"?bref=Num.4.27","r":"Num.4.27","rawR":"Num.4.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.4.27","value":"Num.4.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:27"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["After the initial settlement of Canaan, the Gershonites were allotted 13 cities among the tribes of Issachar, Asher, Naphtali, and Manasseh in the northern part of Palestine (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.6","r":"Josh.21.6","rawR":"Josh.21.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.6","value":"Josh.21.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 21:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["During the time of King David, they were listed among the Levites appointed to service in the temple (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.23.6-11","r":"1Chr.23.6-11","rawR":"1Chr.23.6-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.23.6-11","value":"1Chr.23.6-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 23:6-11"},"). The Gershonite families of Ladan and Jehieli were in charge of the treasury of the house of God (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.26.20-22","r":"1Chr.26.20-22","rawR":"1Chr.26.20-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.26.20-22","value":"1Chr.26.20-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:20-22"},"). At David’s request, music in the temple was directed in part by Asaph and his family, who were Gershonites (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.25.1-2","r":"1Chr.25.1-2","rawR":"1Chr.25.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.25.1-2","value":"1Chr.25.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:1-2"},"). In the reign of King Hezekiah the Gershonites are mentioned among the Levites who cleansed the temple (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.29.1-6,12","r":"2Chr.29.1-6,12","rawR":"2Chr.29.1-6,12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.29.1-6,12","value":"2Chr.29.1-6,12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 29:1-6, 12"},"). In the postexilic period the descendants of Asaph celebrated the laying of the temple foundation (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.3.10","r":"Ezra.3.10","rawR":"Ezra.3.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.3.10","value":"Ezra.3.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 3:10"},") and the dedication of the city walls (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.31-36","r":"Neh.12.31-36","rawR":"Neh.12.31-36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.31-36","value":"Neh.12.31-36"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:31-36"},") with music."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=LeviTribeof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"LeviTribeof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"LeviTribeof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Levi, Tribe of"},"; ",{"href":"?item=PriestsandLevites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"PriestsandLevites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"PriestsandLevites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Priests and Levites"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"GershonGershonites","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 46:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.11","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.11","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.11"},{"anchorText":"Nm 3:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.3.17","rawQueryValue":"Num.3.17","sourceRefExact":"Num.3.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.1","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.1","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.1"},{"anchorText":"Ex 6:16-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.6.16-17","rawQueryValue":"Exod.6.16-17","sourceRefExact":"Exod.6.16-17"},{"anchorText":"Nm 3:18, 21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.3.18,21","rawQueryValue":"Num.3.18,21","sourceRefExact":"Num.3.18,21"},{"anchorText":"Jos 21:1-7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.1-7","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.1-7","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.1-7"},{"anchorText":"Gn 46:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.11","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.11","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.11"},{"anchorText":"Ex 6:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.6.16","rawQueryValue":"Exod.6.16","sourceRefExact":"Exod.6.16"},{"anchorText":"Nm 3:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_